================================================================================================
STEP 1 — WHAT DISTINGUISHES THE ADDITIONAL KEYS' A ROWS (train, multi-key)
================================================================================================

  train B rows with a multi-key label:        6,678
  of those, retrieved top-1 is IN the gold set: 5,564 (83.32%)
  additional gold keys examined:              41,646

  (a) VALUE DATE
      additional key's A rows share the top-1 A row's value date: 99.99%

  (b) AMOUNTS — do they sum toward B?
      top-1's A rows alone equal B's amount exactly:  63.14%
      ALL gold keys' A rows sum to B's amount exactly: 2.59%
      adding the extra rows moves the sum CLOSER to B: 2.25%

  (c) SHARED DIGIT RUNS between additional A rows and the top-1 A row
      share a run of length >= 7: 98.56%

  (d) IS THE SECOND-BEST COSINE CANDIDATE A TRUE ADDITIONAL KEY?
      rows with a distinct rank-2 candidate: 3,879
      rank-2 key is in the gold set:         92.52%
      rank-2 key is a genuinely ADDITIONAL key: 92.52%

  -> value date does not separate them — the additional keys sit on the same date as the top-1, so the date window cannot help
  -> amounts do NOT reliably sum to B, so a subset-sum rule is not available
  -> the rank-2 candidate IS usually a true additional key, which is the signal a completion step can exploit

